{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "That's Christmas To Me feels like a natural choice because Christmas At Downton Abbey gave me a specific interest in seasonal vocal music.",
    "The Best of Bread appeals to my wish for gentle melodies and soft vocals. To All The Girls... also interests me for its vocal duets, although I would preview it before deciding."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Waylon Jennings and Chronicle do not fit the quiet, melodic listening I want now; having some country or older recordings in my history does not make those sounds interchangeable.",
    "Adele, Sam Smith, Motown, indie rock and electronic pop miss the orchestral and polished crossover-vocal qualities I am currently seeking, even when they feature strong singing or familiar songs."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to treat an interest in vocal albums as a broad interest in almost any singer, while the accompaniment and mood matter a great deal to me.",
    "My occasional country and older-pop listening seems to have been stretched into an interest in hits collections across styles, regardless of whether they suit this listening session."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My most recent choice of relaxing classical music deserves more weight because it directly reflects the calm atmosphere I want now.",
    "The repeated soundtrack, stage-song and crossover-vocal choices suggest that expressive voices with orchestral backing are a stronger connection than simply being popular vocal music."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You picked up on my interest in melodic vocals and Christmas music, but spread it too broadly across styles instead of following my current preference for calm classical and crossover listening."
}"}
